# Available Packages and Dependencies

## Core 
### Next.js and React
- next (v15.3.5) — App Router, SSR, API routes
- react (v19.0.0)
- react-dom (v19.0.0)

### UI Framework
- Shadcn
- Emotion (v11.14.x)
  - @emotion/react
  - @emotion/styled

### Data Fetching and State Management
- @tanstack/react-query (v5.81.5) — for all client-side data fetching and caching
- @tanstack/react-query-devtools (v5.81.5) — devtools for React Query
- @tanstack/react-table (latest) — powerful table/data grid functionality for ReUI Data Grid

### Drag and Drop
- @dnd-kit/core (latest) — drag and drop functionality for interactive tables
- @dnd-kit/sortable (latest) — sortable lists and table rows/columns
- @dnd-kit/utilities (latest) — utilities for drag and drop operations

### Utilities
- date-fns (v4.1.0) — date utilities
- lucide-react (v0.525.0) — primary icon library
- uuid (v11.1.0) — unique IDs

### Data Visualization (NEW)
- Recharts (v2.x or latest) — A composable charting library built on React components, ideal for creating interactive and customizable charts for dashboards.

- D3.js (v7.x or latest) — While not a direct React component library, D3 provides powerful low-level primitives for complex, custom data visualizations. Use it judiciously for highly specific or performance-critical charts that Recharts cannot easily achieve.

- Tremor (v2.x or latest) — For ready-to-use, aesthetically pleasing dashboard components and simple charts, designed to be visually appealing out-of-the-box.

### ✨ Animations & Interactions (INSTALLED)
- framer-motion (v12.x or latest) — ✅ INSTALLED - A production-ready motion library for React. It makes adding animations, gestures, and interactive elements to your UI significantly simpler and more performant, crucial for a fluid "bolt.new" feel.
